{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788270324,"nonce":"TbKn5n+rW9wPDTjW3NutbtX2/Jg=","message":"FIXTURE QUESTION 4 IS AFFECTED BY A RENDERER FIX — read before grading a render\nagainst a pre-2026-09-01 image.\n\n`2a7c064` is fixed (`dfcee33`): `baseviz/render.py`'s `_label_pass` was putting\na building's code on the wrong cell, and this issue's fixture question 4 —\n\"check stove cells against the published centre\" — sits directly on it.\n\nThree defects, all closed:\n\n1. `cx = x + (sw*scale)//2` put an ODD-width building's code one cell east.\n   This is what `2a7c064` was filed about, against the 3x1 `ElectricStove` THIS\n   fixture stages.\n2. `cy` had the mirror error — one cell NORTH for an odd HEIGHT — which nobody\n   saw because the specimen's height is 1.\n3. Even-sized rotated buildings had the wrong RECT, because the renderer\n   reproduced only the axis swap from `GenAdj.AdjustForRotation` and dropped\n   its per-axis even-size centre shift.\n\nPlus one in the mod, found because the renderer could not be made correct\nwithout it: `map-dump` published `labels[].rot` through\n`Rot4.ToStringHuman()`, which is **localized** (`\"North\".Translate()`), while\nthe renderer compares it to the literals `\"East\"`/`\"West\"`. On a non-English\ninstall the swap silently never happened. Now `ToStringWord()` (`f947917`,\nassembly rebuilt in `f72f37c`). No change in English.\n\n**Bearing on this spec's scope, and it is small but real:** the PNG channel's\nvalue is being an INDEPENDENT second read, and a labelling offset made a\nplacement error and a rendering error indistinguishable from the image — which\nis the one failure the channel cannot afford. That is now measured rather than\nargued: `accept/2a7c064-label-centre.py`, 20 checks, no bench required.\n\nWhat is NOT done and is why `2a7c064` stays open: nobody has rendered a real\ndump and graded question 4 against it. That is bench work. When this spec's\nfixture next runs, it discharges `2a7c064`'s last bullet as a side effect —\nworth knowing so it is not re-derived.","files":null}]}